(5) Optimize Memory Usage and Data Locality in kdtree_dbscan_OPT
    * Preallocate and Reuse Containers: Instead of allocating new vectors for neighbors in every call to find_neighbors, reuse a preallocated vector. This reduces dynamic memory allocation overhead in your critical loops.
    * Contiguous Data Structures: Ensure your Point3D objects are stored in a cache-friendly layout. For instance, storing coordinates in separate arrays (Structure of Arrays) could further improve cache locality if your access pattern benefits from it.